# Two checks are excluded beyond that base list because they flag Qt's own ownership idioms, not
# a real defect: QVariantMap::operator[] (used throughout the QML bridge to build role data) and
# `new T(parent)` handed to a QObject parent, which Qt's parent/child tree already owns and frees.
Checks: >
  bugprone-*,
  performance-*,
  readability-*,
  modernize-*,
  cppcoreguidelines-*,
  -modernize-use-trailing-return-type,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-avoid-unchecked-container-access,
  -cppcoreguidelines-owning-memory
